.TH PRODBOX_nuke 1
.SH NAME
prodbox-nuke \- Total teardown of every prodbox-owned AWS resource (operator-only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prodbox nuke
.SH DESCRIPTION
The only sanctioned total-decommission path. It executes an Authority-authenticated manifest through the exact exported runner and an acknowledged external receipt; apply fails closed unless the complete production node registry is installed. TTY-only; refuses non-interactive contexts. Requires the typed confirmation literal `NUKE EVERYTHING`; no `--yes` shorthand. `--dry-run` renders the protocol without mutating any state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
Render the teardown plan without mutating state
.TP
\fB--plan-file\fR <PATH>
Write the rendered plan to a file
.TP
\fB--receipt\fR <ABSOLUTE_PATH>
External durable receipt path (required for apply; optional for --dry-run)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBprodbox nuke --dry-run\fR
Render the total-teardown plan.
.TP
\fBprodbox nuke --receipt /operator/decommission/prodbox.receipt\fR
Run with an operator-owned receipt outside every deletion root.
